SEG = "TRA"
CAT = "fqTransport"
Q = [
    ("When a firearm is placed in a vehicle that has a lockable boot, it must be:",
     "Locked in the boot", ["On the back seat in a case", "Under the driver's seat", "In the glove box"],
     "Section 96(2)(a) of the Weapons Regulation 2016 says that if the vehicle has a lockable boot, the weapon must be locked in the boot."),
    ("In a vehicle with no lockable boot, such as a ute, a firearm may be carried:",
     "In a closed case out of sight", ["On a gun rack in the window", "Loose in the open tray", "Across the dashboard, cased"],
     "Section 96(2)(b) allows a securely closed container out of sight in the vehicle, or a locked metal container fixed to the vehicle that does not suggest a weapon is inside."),
    ("A locked metal box fixed to a vehicle for carrying a firearm must not:",
     "Suggest a weapon is inside", ["Be fixed with bolts", "Have a keyed padlock", "Be made of heavy-gauge steel"],
     "Section 96(2)(b)(ii) requires that the metal container and anything on or attached to it does not suggest a weapon is inside. A gun shop sticker or a gun-shaped case would breach this."),
    ("A person in control of a firearm must not leave it in an unlocked vehicle unless:",
     "A licensed person attends it", ["It is parked in daylight", "The firearm is unloaded", "The windows are dark tinted"],
     "Section 96(3) says a weapon must not be left in an unlocked vehicle that is not being attended by someone licensed to possess the weapon. Unloading it does not satisfy the rule."),
    ("A firearm may be dispatched (sent) to someone only if it is:",
     "Unloaded", ["Cleaned", "Registered online", "Fitted with a sling"],
     "Section 97(2) of the Weapons Regulation 2016 says a weapon may be dispatched only if it is unloaded, in a sturdy, securely closed container."),
    ("A private licensee who is not a dealer or armourer may dispatch a firearm only to:",
     "A dealer, armourer or police", ["Any licensed friend", "A shooting club secretary", "A licensed family member"],
     "Under s 97(3), a person who is not a licensed dealer or armourer may dispatch a weapon only to a licensed dealer, a licensed armourer or a police officer acting officially."),
    ("A private licensee who sends a firearm to a dealer must use:",
     "Registered post", ["An ordinary courier", "A parcel locker", "Ordinary letter post"],
     "Section 97(4)(b) of the Weapons Regulation 2016 says anyone other than a licensed dealer may dispatch a weapon only by registered post."),
    ("The outside of a package containing a dispatched firearm must not:",
     "Show it holds a weapon", ["Carry an address", "Be taped shut", "Be made of strong cardboard"],
     "Section 97(6) says the container, and anything on it other than the address, must not suggest a weapon is inside, such as a weapon-shaped box or a label naming a gun shop."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says firearms should be transported:",
     "Unloaded, in a case or bag", ["Loaded with the safety on", "Uncased on a roof rack", "Assembled with the bolt in"],
     "Code principle 8 says all firearms should be transported in a carry case or bag, unloaded, with the bolt removed where applicable."),
    ("When travelling, the National Firearms Safety Code says ammunition must not be carried in:",
     "A magazine that fits the gun", ["Its original box", "A locked container", "A separate locked bag"],
     "The Code says ammunition should be transported in its box and secured, and must not be transported in a magazine that can be fitted to a firearm."),
    ("On an overnight trip, the National Firearms Safety Code says it may be more secure to:",
     "Lock firearms in your room", ["Leave them in the parked car", "Hand them to reception", "Hide them under the car"],
     "The Code says a vehicle should not be considered a secure place to store firearms, and that locking them up in temporary accommodation may be more secure."),
    ("Before taking firearms to another state or territory, the National Firearms Safety Code says to:",
     "Contact that Firearms Registry", ["Contact your safety instructor", "Contact the nearest club", "Contact your insurer only"],
     "Each state and territory has its own firearms laws, so the Code advises contacting the relevant Firearms Registry before travelling interstate."),
    ("Before flying with a firearm, the National Firearms Safety Code says to:",
     "Ask the airline well ahead", ["Pack it in checked luggage", "Carry it on board cased", "Post it ahead to your hotel"],
     "The Code advises contacting the airline well before the departure date to find out how firearms must be submitted for transport."),
    ("When taking a firearm out of a vehicle, the National Firearms Safety Code says to remove it:",
     "Unloaded and butt first", ["Loaded and muzzle first", "Unloaded and muzzle first", "Cased and barrel first"],
     "The Code warns never to remove a firearm muzzle first, because people have shot themselves or companions that way. Make sure it is unloaded and remove it butt first."),
    ("Before getting into a car with a firearm, you should:",
     "Unload it and open the action", ["Engage the safety catch", "Close the bolt on a round", "Put the full magazine back in"],
     "The Code says never take loaded firearms into the car, the home or the camp. Unload, open the action and check there is no ammunition in the breech or magazine."),
    ("For the public place rules in s 57 of the Weapons Act, a public place includes:",
     "A car on a public road", ["A locked private gun room", "Your own fenced paddock", "Your private dwelling"],
     "Section 57(1) says a public place includes a vehicle that is in or on a public place, so a car on a road is covered."),
    ("Under s 57 of the Weapons Act, carrying a weapon in a public place for self-defence is:",
     "Never a reasonable excuse", ["Allowed with a licence", "Allowed after dark only", "Allowed if the gun is unloaded"],
     "Section 57(6) says it is not a reasonable excuse to carry a weapon in a public place for self-defence purposes."),
    ("Without a reasonable excuse, a person must not carry a weapon in a public place:",
     "Exposed to view", ["In a closed case", "Unloaded and locked", "In a car's boot"],
     "Section 57(2) of the Weapons Act makes it an offence to carry a weapon exposed to view in a public place without reasonable excuse, so firearms should be cased."),
    ("Without a reasonable excuse, firing a weapon over a public road in Queensland is:",
     "An offence under s 57", ["Allowed if no cars are near", "Allowed on rural roads", "Allowed for any licensee"],
     "Section 57(4) prohibits discharging a weapon in, into, towards, over or through a public place without reasonable excuse."),
    ("Without a reasonable excuse, carrying a loaded firearm in a public place is:",
     "An offence under s 57", ["Allowed if cased", "Allowed with the safety on", "Allowed on rural roads"],
     "Section 57(3) of the Weapons Act makes it an offence to carry in a public place, without reasonable excuse, a loaded firearm or a weapon capable of being discharged."),
    ("A minor's licence can authorise a minor to physically possess a category A or B weapon to:",
     "Take it to or from a range", ["Carry it for protection", "Hunt alone on any land", "Lend it to a school friend"],
     "Section 36(1)(a) of the Weapons Regulation 2016 lets a minor's licence authorise possession of the weapon to transport it to or from an approved range for that category."),
    ("Under the Weapons Regulation 2016, a licence covers transporting a weapon only when the trip is:",
     "Part of a licensed activity", ["Shorter than 100 km", "Made in daylight hours", "Inside one police district"],
     "Section 6 of the Weapons Regulation 2016 says a licence does not authorise possession of a weapon for transport unless it is necessarily incidental to the activities the licence authorises."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says ammunition in transit should be:",
     "In its box and secured", ["Loose in a jacket pocket", "Loaded in the magazine", "Packed with the firearm"],
     "The Code says ammunition should be transported in its box and secured, and never in a magazine that fits the firearm."),
    ("When a cased firearm is in a car, the National Firearms Safety Code advises keeping the case:",
     "Out of sight", ["On the front seat", "On the roof rack", "Beside an open window"],
     "The Code advises keeping carry cases out of sight in the vehicle where possible, to reduce the risk of theft."),
]
